 ## Exclusions
 
 Exploratory/debug files, local `.olean`/`.ir` artifacts, dependency caches, browser/download scratch files, and work completed after this checkpoint cutoff are excluded. Later or unaccepted work remains excluded, including rational associativity for models outside the literal coefficient family, packaged categorical group objects beyond the proved actual operation diagrams, further basis/count48/Weil identifications and other multiplication-kernel identifications, Hodge evaluation over arbitrary non-domain bases, source Jacobian/factor and polarization identification, general-N torsion and additive/symplectic full-level structure, genus of the contact model, the Gamma-H quotient complex atlas, extension of the admissible level-three comparison across elliptic values and cusps, holomorphic comparison or analytification, and live PEL/source realization. No PR is created by this checkpoint.
+
+The verifier uses the repository's shared Lean source-policy parser. To validate a detached copied progress directory, run the original repository entrypoint with `--root /path/to/copied/progress`; do not execute a copied verifier without the repository scripts. The finite replay passes its copied directory explicitly and still checks every copied source hash and the copied private-inclusive audit. This selector changes only which source directory is inspected, not the validation policy.
